  "body": "This is a place holder for supporting the LR2021.\nThe SX127* series was the first gen chips and had 20dbm with OOK support.\nThe SX126* series was the second gen, got OOK support removed, the reception got better and the output power got to 22dbm\nThe LR1121 is the third gen of the chips and is already supported by RadioLib\nThe LR2021 is the forth gen that got released this week in the press release here: https://www.semtech.com/company/press/semtech-launches-lora-plus-lr2021-transceiver-with-lora-gen-4-technology\n\nThe really great improvement of the LR2021 looks to be TCXO by design and not optional any more. \nSomething many people at Meshtastic would love and change the whole mesh network: Multi-spreading factors (SF) receiver\nOn the one hand this would improve the range by making it possible to use the slowest possible speed when you are far away walking and on the other hand you can use for example the Short Fast mode to have much higher speed and make it possible to get more people on the same frequency.",
